3. Attribution and source sharing
For every shared copy or modified version, retain this license and existing
copyright and attribution notices, identify the upstream repository, state that
you made changes, and include a dated modification log describing those changes.
Provide recipients with the complete corresponding Source of the Project and
your modifications, under this same license, without additional restrictions.
If you share a hosted modified Project, provide an accessible Source link and
the same notices and modification log to its users. Third-party materials keep
their own licenses and must not be relicensed under these terms.

4. Git history and contributions
Use Git commits and the change log for contributions submitted to the upstream
repository. You need not publish private edits, use a particular Git host, or
submit every private commit upstream. Distribution/shared hosting triggers the
source-sharing and modification-log duties in section 3. Contributors must have
the right to license their submitted work under these terms; no ownership
transfer is required. Do not remove historical attribution.

